  "id": "acromegaly",
  "term": "acromegaly",
  "definition": "Acromegaly is a condition in adults caused by long-term excess growth hormone. It leads to enlargement of bones and body parts, especially the face, lower jaw, hands, feet, head, and chest, and is most often linked to a pituitary adenoma that produces growth hormone.",
